WEBVTT

00:00:00.341 --> 00:00:04.053
The two point x integration is a separate desired-state plan and apply

00:00:04.139 --> 00:00:04.608
model.

00:00:04.907 --> 00:00:08.427
Configure its own checkout path, executable and reference.

00:00:08.747 --> 00:00:13.073
Keep Workflows and Scripts one point x on their compatible legacy runtime.

00:00:13.262 --> 00:00:16.142
Runtime recognition only identifies a layout.

00:00:16.376 --> 00:00:20.600
It does not prove that a target provider, resource schema or mutation is

00:00:20.643 --> 00:00:22.088
supported for your environment.

00:00:22.505 --> 00:00:26.472
Open Workflows two point x under Optional Integrations and select the

00:00:26.515 --> 00:00:27.646
intended starter.

00:00:27.923 --> 00:00:31.976
Review the input document, editable global configuration and unique state

00:00:32.062 --> 00:00:32.766
filename.

00:00:33.043 --> 00:00:35.780
Match the installed resource schema and target scope.

00:00:35.958 --> 00:00:38.347
A template selection is not approval.

00:00:38.688 --> 00:00:43.040
Keep state and reviewed inputs associated so later guarded actions cannot

00:00:43.211 --> 00:00:45.899
silently target a different plan or environment.

00:00:46.326 --> 00:00:49.726
Scripts two point x contains converted intent starters.

00:00:50.096 --> 00:00:53.040
They do not execute as the legacy main script command.

00:00:53.424 --> 00:00:56.710
Generate the input and review the corresponding plan in the separate

00:00:56.752 --> 00:00:57.499
runtime.

00:00:57.819 --> 00:01:02.982
P E-only, controller, Foundation and other unmapped legacy actions remain in

00:01:03.024 --> 00:01:04.542
Scripts one point x.

00:01:04.865 --> 00:01:08.862
Do not infer feature parity from similar names across both catalogues.

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:12.886
Submit the plan through the preview workspace and inspect its durable job

00:01:13.057 --> 00:01:14.179
and retained evidence.

00:01:14.619 --> 00:01:19.483
Confirm the target, resource changes, state and supported provider behavior.

00:01:19.739 --> 00:01:23.131
Resolve schema errors and unknowns before considering apply.

00:01:23.408 --> 00:01:27.769
A successful plan does not itself perform or authorize the target change.

00:01:28.119 --> 00:01:31.290
Preserve the exact source and input used to produce it.

00:01:31.575 --> 00:01:35.585
Apply and destroy remain distinct approval-bound actions where the guarded

00:01:35.671 --> 00:01:36.695
lane is enabled.

00:01:36.908 --> 00:01:40.620
Review the exact request and use an authorized environment with a recovery

00:01:40.833 --> 00:01:41.420
path.

00:01:41.793 --> 00:01:45.611
Do not bypass approval or use legacy launchers as a workaround.

00:01:45.889 --> 00:01:48.299
Independently read back the target result.

00:01:48.747 --> 00:01:53.270
Preview status and passing software tests do not establish vendor support or

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:55.508
compatibility for every resource.
